<title>BRAZIL: Brazil central bank losing forex official.</title>
<headline>Brazil central bank losing forex official.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of the international operations department of the Brazilian Central Bank is to retire, an official said.</p>
<p>Joubert Furtado, who has run the bank's operations room on and off for about 30 years and is widely credited with making its dealing desks some of the most market-orientated in Latin America, will remain at the bank for another two weeks.</p>
<p>He had planned to retire in 1999 but recent pension rule changes brought in by a court ruling made hanging on less lucrative, according to the private Invest News agency.</p>
<p>The agency said he would be replaced by Maria do Socorro Costa Carvalho until a permanent new appointment was made.</p>
<p>Furtado was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
